course: dictionary
lesson: 13820
title: The bit before the apostrophe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Isn» is not a word on its own. It is the first part of the short form «isn't», which means «is not». You may see it alone only when the apostrophe and the «t» have been cut off, so always check the whole word.
explain: Short forms join two words into one. In «is not», the letter o is left out, and an apostrophe takes its place: «is not» becomes «isn't». «It isn't fair» means «It is not fair».
explain: Use «isn't» in speech and friendly writing, like «Isn't it lovely?» In a tag question you add it at the end: «It's cold, isn't it?» Read the sentence aloud. If it sounds natural, the short form is right.
fact: «Isn't» is a short form of «is not».
fact: The apostrophe in «isn't» stands where the letter o was left out.
fact: «Isn» alone is only part of a word, so write the whole short form «isn't».
fact: ««It isn't fair» means «It is not fair».»
fact: ««Isn't it lovely?» means «Is it not lovely?»»
exercise: «It isn't fair.» Which two words is «isn't» made from? | *is and not | isn and t | it and is | in and not
exercise: In «isn't», which letter has been left out? | a | *o | e | u
exercise: Tom wrote «isn» in his story. What should it be? | it's | *isn't | isnt | ain't
test: «It's cold, isn't it?» What does «isn't» stand for here? | was not | does not | *is not | will not
test: Which sentence uses the short form correctly? | They isn't here | *The dog isn't here | I isn't ready | Isn't it are lovely
exam: Ali types «isnt» with no apostrophe. Which is the correct form? | *isn't | isn | is'nt | isnt
